  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2 and 3-D SCRUM model and results tuned for the northern Gulf of Alaska shelf",
  "description": "S-coordinate Rutgers University model (Haidvogel), a finite-difference, free-surface model with topography following vertical coordinates. An NPMR project\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Model to understand the dynamic response of the GOA shelf to a distributed coastal buoyancy influx and downwelling winds in support of NPMR \"Process Modeling of the Alaska Coastal Current\"",
